## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an end-to-end, privacy-aware, event-driven pipeline on AWS using basic services.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event triggers and Lambda integration
- Amazon Comprehend for sentiment, entities, and PII
- Redaction patterns and data privacy controls
- Separate storage for redacted transcripts and analytics
- DynamoDB upsert for fast lookups
- IAM, encryption (SSE-KMS), access logs, retries

## Code Example
```javascript
import { ComprehendClient, DetectSentimentCommand, DetectEntitiesCommand, DetectPiiEntitiesCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-comprehend';

const client = new ComprehendClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });

async function analyze(text) {
  const sentiment = await client.send(new DetectSentimentCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  const entities = await client.send(new DetectEntitiesCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  const pii = await client.send(new DetectPiiEntitiesCommand({ Text: text, LanguageCode: 'EN' }));
  return { sentiment: sentiment.Sentiment, entities: entities.Entities, pii: pii.Entities };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement idempotency and retries in the Lambda to avoid duplicates?
- How would you test privacy controls and monitor costs at this scale?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design a simple event-driven image classification pipeline using AWS AI services, with an emphasis on data minimization, role scoping, error handling, and privacy controls.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture (S3, Lambda)
- Rekognition DetectLabels
- Metadata storage alongside assets
- DynamoDB indexing
- DLQ and retries
- Privacy and encryption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda handler sketch for Rekognition calls
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const rek = new AWS.Rekognition();
const s3 = new AWS.S3();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const rec = event.Records[0];
  const bucket = rec.s3.bucket.name;
  const key = rec.s3.object.key;
  const resp = await rek.detectLabels({ Image: { S3Object: { Bucket: bucket, Name: key } }, MaxLabels: 10, MinConfidence: 80 }).promise();
  // Build metadata and upload to same bucket
  const labels = resp.Labels.map(l => ({ name: l.Name, conf: l.Confidence }));
  const metadata = { imageKey: key, labels };
  await s3.putObject({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key.replace(/\.[^/.]+$/, '.metadata.json'), Body: JSON.stringify(metadata) }).promise();
  return labels;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this pipeline locally?
- How would you handle scale and retries for Rekognition calls?

